-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- replay10_verify-R2_r2_merge_unmoved.sql
-- ALLOW_RAW_TESTIMONY_WRITE (fixture rows in the stub tables of a throwaway local cluster, port 55572; never production)
-- R2 (V10-5): photos a merge did NOT move. Live merge_into_primary (sim_merge) moves a duplicate's photo to the survivor
-- stamped merged_from, except a photo whose file the survivor already holds, which stays on the merged-away row; and a
-- photo already on the survivor is never stamped. V1 is merged into V3; then unmerged (sim_unmerge = live unmerge_vehicle).
--   PA: filed on V3 from the start (survivor's own photo); a pass names V1 (its VIN, say).
--   PB: filed on V1, its file already on V3 (twin PB2), so it STAYS on V1; a pass names the survivor V3.
--   PM: filed on V1, moved by the merge (control: the v10 fix's case); a pass names V3.
-- He confirms each while merged (p_expected = the photo's filing he sees). After the unmerge, where do his yeses sit?
-- Local scratch only (verifier verify-R2, port 55572). Generated ids, never production.
-- ALLOW_RAW_TESTIMONY_WRITE (fixture rows in the stub tables of a throwaway cluster)
-- Actors as PostgREST makes them (scenario_v10's idiom): session authenticator + role + request.jwt.claims.
\pset pager off
\pset format unaligned
\pset tuples_only on
SET client_min_messages = warning;
RESET ROLE; RESET SESSION AUTHORIZATION;
